    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0764" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg704"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Viscount Gough to Mr. Uhl</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Newport</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-07-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, the receipt of your note, No. 143, of the 3d instant, respecting the
                    apparently conflicting claims of territorial jurisdiction over certain islands
                    in Lac de Croix, on the northwestern boundary between Minnesota and Manitoba. I
                    have not failed to bring your communication to the notice of Her Majesty’s
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gough</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
